[Music]  welcome to cloud on air  live webinars from google cloud we are  hosting webinars daily  you are watching cloud 101 where we  discuss the fundamental concept of  google cloud platform  and learn from the best practices in  different markets  my name is anuj and today we will be  talking about how to manage chrome  browser from the cloud  you can ask questions anytime on the  platform and we have googlers on standby  to answer them  let's get started before we dive in  let's talk about the importance of the  browser the browser is about more than  productivity  with the rise of cloud-based enterprise  applications  more and more enterprise data is flowing  through the browser  that data needs to be secured and  mitigating security risks  is a top priority for enterprises  for some enterprises the need to manage  the browser comes from a compliance or  regulatory perspective  enterprises operating in heavily  regulated markets will often lock down  specific features of the browser  to reduce risk or enforce business needs  with the bulk of enterprise user  activity shifting to the web  the browser needs to play an active role  in the enterprise's security posture  today we'll discuss how the browser  plays a large part in user productivity  and enterprise security  here are the topics that we'll be going  over in our webinar today  first i'll talk about some of the  benefits of managing chrome  and why enterprises are increasingly  making use of chrome's management  features  then i'll cover chrome management  options that we offer today  third i'll introduce chrome browser  cloud management a brand new option for  managing chrome from the cloud  that we're making available for ev to  everyone  and finally i'll walk you through a demo  of its core features  the way we work is changing and the  evolving role of the web and enterprises  has a large part to play in this  more and more work today is done on the  web thanks to the richness of the  enterprise software as a service  ecosystem  that's grown and the web platform that  powers it  in that context the browser is quickly  becoming the centerpiece  for the delivery of business critical  applications  as you can see from the statistics here  both it administrators  and it workers are seeing this shift  first hand  73 percent of enterprises agree that the  browser has become more important to  their it strategy  65 percent of workers report relying  more heavily on their browser today  than they did two years ago so in many  cases it's about making your enterprise  users more productive  that's also where management comes in  administrators can configure the browser  to work  optimally for their environments from  having the right printing defaults  configured automatically  to installing the right extension for  their video conferencing provider  and that's why we need to manage the  browser it's a great way to achieve your  enterprise's productivity compliance and  security goals  chrome supports a very rich set of  browser policies and as  an administrator you have access to  hundreds of browser policies that allow  you to configure  almost any aspect of chrome here are  some examples of where enterprises  often rely on browser policies to  achieve their business goals  first is managing extensions enterprise  admins want to be able to  enable or disable extensions based on  their enterprise needs  control what types of permissions an  extension can request  and send customized messages to  employees when they try to install  extensions that aren't allowed  deploying preset options can make the  browser feel more integrated into your  enterprise  the right certificates proxy settings  and services can be configured by the  admin  so that the browser just works by  default  controlling updates ensures that the  browser is up-to-date  and protected from vulnerabilities and  last but not least  as i mentioned before chrome supports  a very rich set of browser policies and  as an administrator you have access to  hundreds of browser policies  that allow you to control every aspect  of chrome  so today enterprises have two options  for managing chrome  first is to use your platform's existing  management tools to set chrome policies  if you manage windows services you can  set policies using microsoft's  software excuse me microsoft's group  policy objects to configure software on  windows  we offer admx templates to make it easy  to set policies on windows  and we offer options that are  appropriate for mac os  and linux second for enterprises that  already have g suite or have adopted  google identity  those customers can use google admin  console to set user policies  when their users sign into chrome chrome  fetches and applies those user policies  but each of these approaches have their  own set of drawbacks  with existing management tools a simple  apology a policy change  that needs to be applied across windows  mac and linux might take three different  administrators  three different tools and three  different deployment cycles  it's a lot of extra work just to set a  single policy  and also when admins rely on user  profiles  that means that employees have to sign  into chrome to apply the policies  and not every enterprise wants to use  profiles where users have to sign in  to solve these challenges we created  chrome browser cloud management which is  an  easier way to manage chrome deployments  of any size  from a central cloud location across  windows  mac and linux it's also easy to  implement  your end users do not need google  accounts to receive policies  and there is no need for your end users  to sign into the browser  you'll also gain deeper insights into  your deployment  with this new feature admins can  immediately see information about the  policies that are set  the current versions of the browser and  even which extensions are installed  the best part is that all this  information is available from a simple  web console  so if you're an existing g suite  customer you can get started  right away by signing into the google  admin console at  admin.google.com and navigating to the  device management pages  and selecting manage browsers you'll  find instructions on how to enroll  browsers  and get started on that page if your  enterprise has purchased  chrome browser enterprise support or  have  chrome enterprise licenses your admin  console  also has this new service provision  similarly if you've provisioned google  cloud identity  your admin console also already has this  service provisioned  if your enterprise doesn't have g suite  or they don't use  other google services you can still test  this feature  at no charge at the link listed here  we'll also display this information  again at the end of the webinar  so enrolling browsers into chrome  browser cloud management is super easy  once your administrator account is  created you can sign into the google  admin console  navigate to the browser management pages  and create your organizational unit  structure  once your structure is created you can  retrieve your enrollment token for the  organizational unit  that you would like to enroll browsers  into  with that token you will use your  existing tools to set one last platform  policy on the devices  running the browsers that you want to  enroll once that token is set  the browser will enroll itself into the  google admin console  receive browser policies from the cloud  and you can choose to enable the  optional cloud reporting functionality  which will send some information  about the state of your browser  deployment to the admin console  now i'll give you a first-hand look at  the administrator experience  for chrome browser cloud management  in this first video you'll see how to  retrieve an enrollment token from the  console  here the administrator is already logged  into the google admin console  and you'll see them perform a few steps  first they'll navigate to the browser  list page  by locating the manage browser cards in  the device management section  once they've landed on the browser list  page it will list the currently enrolled  browsers  and finally by clicking on the yellow  button they'll retrieve an enrollment  token for one of the organizational  units  that has already been configured  next we'll take a closer look at the  sorting  and filtering options that are available  on the browser list page  from the device list page we can use  search and sorting to quickly get  insight into the state of the fleet  we'll sort by browser version to find  chrome browsers that haven't been  updated in a while  those machines might be good candidates  for applying the forced restart policy  that helps ensure  that chrome stays up to date at a  reasonable pace  in this view we'll go over some of the  browser details that you can obtain  if you choose to turn on the optional  cloud reporting feature  you'll be able to view the extensions  that are installed  which policies are set on the specific  browser  and what plugins are installed  here you can see that the admin has  clicked into  a specific machine and they have a lot  of information available to them  about this machine you can see the  extensions that are installed  which policies are set on this specific  browser  and which plugins are installed  very good information  in our last demo we'll take a look at  the browser extension list page  this page is particularly handy if you  want to get an overview of the  extensions that  your enterprise end users have installed  across your fleet  first we'll look at the browser  extensions list  we can see how many times an extension  has been installed  and we can even force install extensions  you can see we're force installing the  dock extensions  now  next you'll see how to set a new browser  policy in an organizational unit with  chrome browser cloud management  we'll navigate to the browser policy  page  then we'll give you a quick overview of  the types of policies that you can set  and then you can use the search box to  find  cloud reporting user setting and turn it  on  for the whole organization  this will install an optional extension  that you can use to get more insight  into your browser deployment  adding this extension is what gets a lot  of the data and information that you've  been seeing in the demo so far  including the extensions list page  so chrome browser cloud management  enables you to see a ton of data about  your organization  and this service has its own terms that  are compatible with google's  google cloud's other services we also  offer a data export service that allows  you to take your data with you at any  time  deleting a browser results in the  associated information being deleted  from the admin console's storage system  your data is yours to keep  so what's in store for chrome browser  cloud management  well we already support a very rich set  of policies in the admin console  and we want to make even more of the 300  plus policies that we support today  configurable from the cloud in  particular  we want to bring cloud policy controls  for enterprise specific features  such as legacy browser support and for  managing updates  into admin console additionally  we've heard from customers that controls  around enterprise security  such as password alert are important so  we want to bring these features into the  admin console as well  that concludes our quick tour of chrome  browser  cloud management it gives you a quick  way to manage chrome  across windows mac and linux it gives  you great insights into your browser  deployment  and it gives you the ability to delegate  browser management  separately from other management work  you can get started today by visiting g  dot co  chrome cloud management  we also have a wealth of resources to  support you as you deploy  and manage chrome there are two in  particular that i'd like to point out  enterprise release notes we offer a very  rich set of enterprise specific release  notes  at every chrome release if you're an  enterprise admin that wants to stay  abreast of changes in chrome  this is an excellent way to do just that  additionally our website at chrome.com  enterprise contains a ton of information  about how you can manage chrome in your  organization  and with that thank you for attending  our webinar if you'd like to get started  with chrome browser cloud management  please visit g.co chrome cloud  management  thank you for tuning in please visit  cloud on air for more content from  google cloud experts  [Music]  you

